        "method": "Published author proof/core and local context fidelity screening",
        "note": "Select Theorem4.4 with its original hypotheses: X smooth projective minimal surface of general type, k positive, L (k-1)-very ample, chi(L)>=3k and L.K>=2K^2+k+1. Additionally select the explicit Lemma4.1 branch in which m=L.K-2K^2, n=(L-K)^2+3chi(OX)-4k-1 and p=K^2-chi(OX)+3 are all even and n>=0. The complete Claim4.2 residue transformations and its coefficient convolution then supply the new sign core; the three other parity branches whose details are left to the reader are not selected. Full Theorem4.4 numerical reduction, Noether-inequality use and Segre residue substitution4.2 are included. Universal Segre formula4.1 and the established big/nef criterion for a globally generated bundle are author-cited background. No K3, Enriques, blowup or curve variant is separately counted."
